    "operationId": "webhookReceiveDelete",
    "summary": "Capture an inbound webhook (DELETE)",
    "description": "Point the system under test's webhook URL here. Stores the whole request - method, query parameters (other than key and status), headers, source IP, and body - under the namespace key. JSON bodies are also returned parsed as 'json'; non-UTF-8 bodies are kept as bodyBase64. Bodies over 300 KB are truncated (bodyTruncated:true). No pre-registration: any key works. Answers with HTTP 'status' (default 200) so you can test the sender's retry behaviour. Accepts GET, POST, PUT, PATCH and DELETE. Captured events expire after 30 days.",
